{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"75a4e4ea852c82c7","type":"text","text":"**Angaidh/Angie Vauclair**\nMansteri, pretending (succesfully) to be a Lagainian. Is avoiding the bloodtithe by doing so. Wants to start a successful merchantile business in the barony of Gwen and is also going to use it to smuggle supplies/artifacts out of the place and to the Marathan researchers. \n\nSays she is from Lenz, actually from Lochia.\n\nA lady of means from Lenz who is here, accompanied by **Neeve Marchand**, to investigate its potential as a base of operations for another arm of her family's business that seems to involve the transport of other merchant's goods. They were childhood friends that met on their first pilgrimage up the Starcairn and who were both born under the same sign (Garuda).\n\nAs Lailah gets to know her, she explains she was originally sent to a monastery near the Starcairn, but was recalled to rejoin her family after the deaths of several of her older brothers and sisters. Eventually this lead to Angie learning how to keep books for the purposes of maintaining the family's estate, but this grew into more of an enterprise as she sought means of shoring them up after dwindling funds became apparent. Previously, her family had in part funded a portion of the defense of the barony against Tousav, but the ties there had died out and with the replacement of the baron at the end of the war, she saw an opportunity to build them anew. Recently she has begun to claim that the first shipments are already set to arrive and wishes greatly to see the marketplace built soon so that she may send back the fruits of this land's untapped potential as proof greater investment would be foolhardy to not pursue. She's quite adamant this will occur and claims her new connections are already bountiful, citing Lailah as one of them.\n\n![[Pasted image 20260526194432.png]]","x":522,"y":-78,"width":778,"height":678},
		{"id":"1adec70a3786dc98","type":"text","text":"She has been getting relics from here and shipping them to Mansteri/Marathan operatives under the guise of mercantile business.","x":100,"y":-378,"width":250,"height":192},
		{"id":"255398befa97c33d","type":"text","text":"**Iron Mine**\nWas gradually dwindling, but now has completely shut down after being attacked by old head's big mad son.","x":-2692,"y":-1814,"width":372,"height":174},
		{"id":"799fa0ec226dbc0f","type":"text","text":"**Baron Hywel**\nDisplaced the old guy. Want's all of the old guy's stuff.","x":-1460,"y":-1560,"width":250,"height":187},
		{"id":"d3d7726e3ed6812d","type":"text","text":"**Old Head's Son**\nHas his dad's sword and is attempting to fruitlessly use it to stir up riots against the new baron, but people don't mind him.","x":-2692,"y":-1160,"width":372,"height":134},
		{"id":"398df1e5c314f3ac","type":"text","text":"**The Tower**\nAn ancient Marathan astronomy tower that was reused by the barony as a fire tower. It lay unused for years before being taken over by bandits to scout out plumes of smoke of incoming pilgrims.","x":25,"y":-760,"width":400,"height":194},
		{"id":"624ac5f1aba55f49","type":"text","text":"**The Gate of the Laborer Mikalaeon**\n\nLarge Gate built here in order to support efforts going forward for the creation of research centers and facilities. The keystone has been thrown far into the forest and requires some navigating to retrieve the three pieces. It is currently exuding some effects on the surrounding landscape:\n- Highly stable. Things like the grass and branches are reinforced heavily.\n- Occasionally constructing pillars and holes\n- Shoving people around, perhaps into something dangerous","x":-680,"y":-1038,"width":585,"height":278},
		{"id":"c0574c21244d4de0","type":"text","text":"**Zarrin**\nBaron's man, supplied him and others with drugs (sweetleaf and irongnaw) for a long time while everyone was locked up, eventually got pulled into the penal colony himself.\n\nSees himself as descended from 2nd Age ancestors rather than his Marathan (Ansium) heritage. Wants to figure out how to gain thaumaturgy without making his own personal sacrifice.","x":-1575,"y":-1020,"width":480,"height":260},
		{"id":"0223ebe6f60408dd","type":"text","text":"**Niamh/Neeve Marchand**\nMet Angie on the Starcairn, from Lenz.","x":786,"y":-282,"width":250,"height":124},
		{"id":"b8c46322d0b71b36","type":"text","text":"**Uillean/William le Goff**\nLaborer who is actually a Marathan (Puradi) thaumaturge. Keeping an eye on the other Mansteri operatives and trying to sniff out potential threats. Claims to be a lumberer who scouts out particularly robust trees for ship building  (sterns, masts, etc.).\n\nA respectful, if quiet, fellow that is originally from Puradi. He's found his way up here in order to take advantage of the cheap sale of large lumber in the use of shipbuilding. Despite his strange heritage, he claims to be a half-blooded Lagainian and wishes to follow in his mother's footsteps, but is unsure of where to begin.","x":522,"y":640,"width":778,"height":280},
		{"id":"2d85665c3d809108","type":"text","text":"**Tearlach/Charles Clerce** ","x":522,"y":960,"width":778,"height":240},
		{"id":"20c335cdbde416af","type":"text","text":"**Aveline Rousseau**\nA seamstress and handmaid from Holy Caledon. Was a handmaid for a noble headed here, but at the noble's passing on the journey was dismissed from her work. Feeling quite lost and hoping to find another noble to follow.\n\nA seamstress and, previously, a handmaid traveling out here at the side of her lady all the way from Holy Caledon. Unfortunately, during the trip, her elderly matron passed on. Her handmaid (Aveline) completed the trip and now awaits missive back from her house in Lagain.","x":-1000,"y":402,"width":480,"height":318},
		{"id":"633b991afb6df164","type":"text","text":"**Eero Erinsol**\nA true Lagainian faith believer from Graland. He's answering the call to arms put out by Lagainians and hoping to send money back home to his wife.\n\nHe works hard for the barony as a mason and prays on his time off, oftentimes being overly earnest in his faith. He seems near penitent for some unspoken crime, but speaks fondly of a wife waiting for him back home in Graland. He's frequently asking around for people to help him write letters to send back to her.","x":-1000,"y":780,"width":480,"height":300}
	],
